\section{Session Types and Object-Oriented Programming}\label{sec:session-oo}

Session types can be integrated with object-oriented programming to specify communication protocols for objects.

\subsection{Class-Based Session Types}\label{sec:class-session}

In a class-based language, each class can declare the session types of its communication channels:

\begin{verbatim}
  class Server {
    session: ?Request.!Response.*   // receive request, send response, repeat
    handle() {
      loop {
        let req = self.channel.receive()
        let resp = process(req)
        self.channel.send(resp)
      }
    }
  }
\end{verbatim}

\subsection{Actor Model and Session Types}\label{sec:actor-session}

The actor model of concurrent computation can be enhanced with session types to provide protocol guarantees:

\begin{itemize}
  \item Each actor has a session type describing its communication protocol.
  \item Messages between actors must conform to the session types.
  \item The type checker verifies that all actors follow their protocols.
\end{itemize}

