\subsection{Verification of Session-Typed Programs}\label{sec:session-verification-adv}

Session types can be combined with verification frameworks for stronger guarantees:

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Model checking.} Verify that the session type is free from deadlocks and livelocks.
  \item \textbf{Theorem proving.} Prove that the protocol satisfies application-specific properties (e.g., the total amount transferred is correct).
  \item \textbf{Runtime monitoring.} Check protocol conformance at runtime for dynamically-typed protocols.
\end{itemize}

\begin{verbatim}
  -- Verified session type in F*:
  val transfer: amount:int{amount > 0} ->
    unit ST (requires (fun h -> balance h >= amount))
            (ensures (fun h0 _ h1 -> balance h1 == balance h0 - amount))
  -- The transfer operation is verified to preserve the balance invariant
\end{verbatim}

